ive litres of blood so let's multiply  this times five liters per human per  average human obviously a small human  will have less and and a very large  person will have more blood flowing  through them but this is an average  person right over here so then we get  the liters cancel out  and so we get 0.8 times five eight times  five is forty point eight times five and  have one decimal place it's going to be  four eight point eight times five is  four and then we have grams per human  four grams per human and just to get an  idea of what four grams all are one  teaspoon 1 teaspoon 1 teaspoon is equal  to four point two grams so four grams is  almost a teaspoon so it's approximately  it's approximately one teaspoon 1  teaspoon of glucose per human being so  in your entire bloodstream you have  about a teaspoon of sugar that your  cells can use to do whatever cells need  to do
 

